# This project publishes everything it can. The list below is short on purpose, and every line has a reason
# that is about size or about the file being machine-made noise -- never about hiding a result. If you are
# looking for the evidence behind a number in the blog, it is in the repository: every run's config.json,
# result.json, log.csv, samples.txt and evaluation-*.json are committed, and so are the token streams.

# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Model weights, and ONLY the weights. Each checkpoint is 43 to 141 MB and there are 62 of them, 7.8 GB in all;
# GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB outright and asks you not to push files over 50 MB. So the weights of the
# released model go to Hugging Face, where large files are the point, and the rest stay on the machine that made
# them. Everything a checkpoint can tell you -- its configuration, its scores, its whole training log, the text it
# writes -- is committed beside it in plain text.
*.pt
*.safetensors

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
